      "subject": "fix(executive): the Chief Agent reasons with all current-policy knowledge, not a word match (KA-1, F-27)",
      "body": "When a question was asked, the knowledge context builder kept only canonical items whose title or summary shared a word with it. Summaries are generic, so governing documents were dropped before reasoning: for 'which pending canonical review should I handle first' the Chief Agent received 8 of 26 current-policy items and never saw the Platform Constitution, Business Charter, Blueprint, Vision 2050 or its own architecture. The executive context now asks for retrieval all; the governed content reader already ranks certified document text by the question within its budget, which is how KO-6 intended ranking to work. Other callers keep the default search.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AHtXdN7VRusNxTFHzk5uFe",
